# Cross-architecture cross-MCU stepper validation -- atmega2560 X/Y +
# stm32f103 Z. Like multi_mcu_avr_stm32.test, but stepper_z's pins
# live on the renode-backed satellite via `other:`-prefixed pin
# values. G28 has to home Z by emitting a step_trigger command on the
# renode bridge's control socket (translated into a Python call to
# renode_hooks.step_trigger() that registers a Renode GPIO StateChanged
# hook), while X/Y step_triggers fire on the simavr bridge. If the
# fixture pusher routes the Z step_trigger to the wrong bridge -- or
# skips the prefixed pins entirely as the pre-MCU-aware pusher would
# -- Z homing would hang until klippy's home_wait timeout fires.
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict other=stm32f103.dict
CONFIG multi_mcu_avr_stm32_xmcu.cfg
EMULATOR multi_mcu_avr_stm32_xmcu.fixture.json

G28
M114

EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'other'"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
